_choice","config":{"sat_topic":"Standard English Conventions"},"points":1,"required":true,"group_name":"Form, Structure, and Sense"},{"id":"36f1035c-5358-47c4-be29-94a87a5d65fa","test_id":"9c4d7708-f642-5cca-9458-57c66aa2f1b7","prompt":"She had reviewed the entire draft before she ___ her comments. Which choice completes the sentence?","options":["has submitted","will submit","submitted","submits"],"position":10,"type":"multiple_choice","config":{"sat_topic":"Standard English Conventions"},"points":1,"required":true,"group_name":"Form, Structure, and Sense"},{"id":"162f0e28-f0e2-42a0-87bf-9514c0a6c2fa","test_id":"9c4d7708-f642-5cca-9458-57c66aa2f1b7","prompt":"The students were given two choices: ___ the existing design or propose a new one. Which choice completes the sentence?","options":["had revised","revise","revised","revising"],"position":11,"type":"multiple_choice","config":{"sat_topic":"Standard English Conventions"},"points":1,"required":true,"group_name":"Form, Structure, and Sense"},{"id":"504e367d-067b-4f03-a24a-11f129269c7d","test_id":"9c4d7708-f642-5cca-9458-57c66aa2f1b7","prompt":"The team tested the battery twice; ___, it remained unsure of the result. Which choice completes the sentence?","options":["however","therefore","for example","similarly"],"position":12,"type":"multiple_choice","config":{"sat_topic":"Expression of Ideas"},"points":1,"required":true,"group_name":"Transitions"},{"id":"7c0c963b-192a-43d6-9f25-f15dcc3cbdd6","test_id":"9c4d7708-f642-5cca-9458-57c66aa2f1b7","prompt":"Demand fell sharply. ___, the factory reduced production. Which choice completes the sentence?","options":["Nevertheless","For instance","In contrast","Consequently"],"position":13,"type":"multiple_choice","config":{"sat_topic":"Expression of Ideas"},"points":1,"required":true,"group_name":"Transitions"},{"id":"6dd982e4-91b3-4578-9931-7097b1f64ac9","test_id":"9c4d7708-f642-5cca-9458-57c66aa2f1b7","prompt":"The author cites two examples of urban adaptation. ___, some plants flower earlier in warmer city centers. Which choice completes the sentence?","options":["Instead","Conversely","For instance","Nevertheless"],"position":14,"type":"multiple_choice","config":{"sat_topic":"Expression of Ideas"},"points":1,"required":true,"group_name":"Transitions"},{"id":"50d88030-90f2-471d-a21e-bccbd356ff81","test_id":"9c4d7708-f642-5cca-9458-57c66aa2f1b7","prompt":"The river was usually shallow. ___, after days of heavy rain, it overflowed. Which choice completes the sentence?","options":["In other words","However","Similarly","For this reason"],"position":15,"type":"multiple_choice","config":{"sat_topic":"Expression of Ideas"},"points":1,"required":true,"group_name":"Transitions"},{"id":"d8d9d8b8-7578-4c36-93da-79c1e9e4e702","test_id":"9c4d7708-f642-5cca-9458-57c66aa2f1b7","prompt":"The first survey measured travel time. ___, the second measured fuel use rather than time. Which choice completes the sentence?","options":["By contrast","Consequently","For example","Indeed"],"position":16,"type":"multiple_choice","config":{"sat_topic":"Expression of Ideas"},"points":1,"required":true,"group_name":"Transitions"},{"id":"7c080486-8847-488c-bd6e-7a1c33fa237f","test_id":"9c4d7708-f642-5cca-9458-57c66aa2f1b7","prompt":"Three species returned after the wetland was restored. ___, the area now supports more species than before. Which choice completes the sentence?","options":["Nevertheless","By contrast","For instance","As a result"],"position":17,"type":"multiple_choice","config":{"sat_topic":"Expression of Ideas"},"points":1,"required":true,"group_name":"Transitions"},{"id":"94aea736-9d3f-4d15-a8ca-e7201f2bd323","test_id":"9c4d7708-f642-5cca-9458-57c66aa2f1b7","prompt":"A filter removed most large particles but allowed smaller particles to pass. A second filter caught most of those smaller particles.\n\nHow did the second filter improve the system?","options":["It reduced the number of large particles entering the system.","It replaced the need for filtration.","It captured particles the first filter missed.","It released particles from the first filter."],"position":18,"type":"multiple_choice","config":{"sat_topic":"Information and Ideas"},"points":1,"required":true,"group_name":"Main Ideas and Details"},{"id":"0d11cac1-8609-428f-a0bb-eb352f058ac1","test_id":"9c4d7708-f642-5cca-9458-57c66aa2f1b7","prompt":"A city reduced its bus fares while increasing the frequency of service. Ridership increased over the next quarter.\n\nWhy can the increase not be attributed to fares alone?","options":["The fare change preceded the service change by years.","Service frequency changed at the same time.","The city increased its fares.","Ridership was not measured."],"position":19,"type":"multiple_choice","config":{"sat_topic":"Information and Ideas"},"points":1,"required":true,"group_name":"Inference"},{"id":"ccf123f7-493f-4035-954a-578db048f326","test_id":"9c4d7708-f642-5cca-9458-57c66aa2f1b7","prompt":"Some artists in the exhibition use discarded materials to reduce waste. Others choose those materials because their irregular shapes invite experimentation.\n\nWhat does the text emphasize?","options":["Artists can choose the same materials for different reasons.","All artists in the exhibition share the same goal.","Discarded materials limit experimentation.","Only irregular materials reduce waste."],"position":20,"type":"multiple_choice","config":{"sat_topic":"Information and Ideas"},"points":1,"required":true,"group_name":"Main Ideas and Details"},{"id":"ac8388ef-e523-4e5d-b96f-786abf79b14f","test_id":"9c4d7708-f642-5cca-9458-57c66aa2f1b7","prompt":"The first night’s measurements were discarded because the instrument had been exposed to rain. Later measurements were taken under a protective cover.\n\nWhy were the first measurements discarded?","options":["The protective cover changed the weather.","The later measurements were unavailable.","The experiment required a sunny location.","Rain may have affected the instrument."],"position":21,"type":"multiple_choice","config":{"sat_topic":"Information and Ideas"},"points":1,"required":true,"group_name":"Main Ideas and Details"},{"id":"1d1ac4ff-33f3-42e6-b556-4483bb7bb0af","test_id":"9c4d7708-f642-5cca-9458-57c66aa2f1b7","prompt":"A local newspaper published a weekly column about transit improvements. Its writers focused on proposals that had been funded and excluded proposals still under debate.\n\nWhich proposal would most likely appear in the column?","options":["A bus route under discussion with no budget.","A petition asking the city to consider a bridge.","A funded upgrade to a tram stop.","An unfunded idea for a new railway."],"position":22,"type":"multiple_choice","config":{"sat_topic":"Information and Ideas"},"points":1,"required":true,"group_name":"Inference"},{"id":"fb7b9711-43ef-4537-9b94-ffc8ce7db7ed","test_id":"9c4d7708-f642-5cca-9458-57c66aa2f1b7","prompt":"The village installed meters on all public taps. Officials later found that most of the water loss came from a single damaged pipe.\n\nWhat did officials find?","options":["Water loss was unrelated to the pipe network.","One damaged pipe accounted for most of the loss.","Public taps had not been fitted with meters.","Most of the loss came from many small leaks."],"position":23,"type":"multiple_choice","config":{"sat_topic":"Information and Ideas"},"points":1,"required":true,"group_name":"Main Ideas and Details"},{"id":"1fbe123c-9112-4fa1-92ba-bd91417f804d","test_id":"9c4d7708-f642-5cca-9458-57c66aa2f1b7","prompt":"The author describes the machine first as surprisingly simple and later as difficult to repair without specialized tools.\n\nWhat distinction does the author make?","options":["Simple design does not guarantee easy repair.","Complex design always makes repair impossible.","Specialized tools simplify the original design.","The machine was repaired easily by the author."],"position":24,"type":"multiple_choice","config":{"sat_topic":"Information and Ideas"},"points":1,"required":true,"group_name":"Main Ideas and Details"},{"id":"e766f48d-4726-4f07-8be7-f177f79f22b2","test_id":"9c4d7708-f642-5cca-9458-57c66aa2f1b7","prompt":"In a field trial, a reflective coating lowered roof temperatures during sunny afternoons. The study recorded no readings after dark.\n\nWhat question cannot be answered from the trial?","options":["Whether the trial took place outdoors.","When the recorded cooling occurred.","Whether the coating was reflective.","How the coating affects roof temperatures at night."],"position":25,"type":"multiple_choice","config":{"sat_topic":"Information and Ideas"},"points":1,"required":true,"group_name":"Inference"},{"id":"cbcd13ef-76b2-4f5d-9b5d-c30dad7f3a77","test_id":"9c4d7708-f642-5cca-9458-57c66aa2f1b7","prompt":"A tree inventory revealed that just two species accounted for most trees on a single street. The city plans to plant more species there.\n\nWhat goal does the plan most directly serve?","options":["Measuring the age of the existing trees.","Removing every tree from the street.","Increasing the diversity of street trees.","Reducing the number of species on the street."],"position":26,"type":"multiple_choice","config":{"sat_topic":"Information and Ideas"},"points":1,"required":true,"group_name":"Inference"},{"id":"71ebab70-eb55-45d7-bcd6-9999e9c9c0e5","test_id":"e4b994df-8f8f-582a-bba2-e53c002d825a","prompt":"The bridge remained operational throughout the storm. In this sentence, what does “operational” most nearly mean?","options":["functional","fragile","temporary","hidden"],"position":0,"type":"multiple_choice","config":{"sat_topic":"Craft and Structure"},"points":1,"required":true,"group_name":"Words in Context"},{"id":"ec8becfb-366e-46e7-a937-e08d1a366a65","test_id":"e4b994df-8f8f-582a-bba2-e53c002d825a","prompt":"A second survey corroborated the team’s initial findings. In this sentence, what does “corroborated” most nearly mean?","options":["replaced","distorted","ignored","confirmed"],"position":1,"type":"multiple_choice","config":{"sat_topic":"Craft and Structure"},"points":1,"required":true,"group_name":"Words in Context"},{"id":"a33647bf-b5f7-41b8-9840-e6bfda05ed90","test_id":"e4b994df-8f8f-582a-bba2-e53c002d825a","prompt":"The once abundant plant is now scarce. In this sentence, what does “scarce” most nearly mean?","options":["widespread","cultivated","rare","hardy"],"position":2,"type":"multiple_choice","config":{"sat_topic":"Craft and Structure"},"points":1,"required":true,"group_name":"Words in Context"},{"id":"014533ee-50f4-46d2-bbf0-2faf608b89ca","test_id":"e4b994df-8f8f-582a-bba2-e53c002d825a","prompt":"The new insulation mitigated the effects of cold weather. In this sentence, what does “mitigated” most nearly mean?","options":["reversed","reduced","measured","predicted"],"position":3,"type":"multiple_choice","config":{"sat_topic":"Craft and Structure"},"points":1,"required":true,"group_name":"Words in Context"},{"id":"3355d3a0-1355-44fd-b740-6ac4c9a0e924","test_id":"e4b994df-8f8f-582a-bba2-e53c002d825a","prompt":"The architect retained the original façade. In this sentence, what does “retained” most nearly mean?","options":["kept","photographed","removed","redesigned"],"position":4,"type":"multiple_choice","config":{"sat_topic":"Craft and Structure"},"points":1,"required":true,"group_name":"Words in Context"},{"id":"a27e6b2f-fe81-42d3-ad18-50a3bd249273","test_id":"e4b994df-8f8f-582a-bba2-e53c002d825a","prompt":"The editor requested a concise account of the event. In this sentence, what does “concise” most nearly mean?","options":["dramatic","incomplete","speculative","brief"],"position":5,"type":"multiple_choice","config":{"sat_topic":"Craft and Structure"},"points":1,"required":true,"group_name":"Words in Context"},{"id":"26e418de-f78a-4079-986d-5a223a398751","test_id":"e4b994df-8f8f-582a-bba2-e53c002d825a","prompt":"The results were preliminary and could change with further analysis. In this sentence, what does “preliminary” most nearly mean?","opti