2-e53c002d825a","prompt":"The paintings in the west gallery ___ to the nineteenth century. Which choice completes the sentence?","options":["is dating","date","dates","has dated"],"position":11,"type":"multiple_choice","config":{"sat_topic":"Standard English Conventions"},"points":1,"required":true,"group_name":"Form, Structure, and Sense"},{"id":"721e52c9-8ec2-42d0-a392-116af6e71192","test_id":"e4b994df-8f8f-582a-bba2-e53c002d825a","prompt":"A series of workshops ___ scheduled for the spring. Which choice completes the sentence?","options":["is","are","have been","were"],"position":12,"type":"multiple_choice","config":{"sat_topic":"Standard English Conventions"},"points":1,"required":true,"group_name":"Form, Structure, and Sense"},{"id":"56361ec5-d758-4f0b-9741-f18795568d0e","test_id":"e4b994df-8f8f-582a-bba2-e53c002d825a","prompt":"If the team had started earlier, it ___ the survey before sunset. Which choice completes the sentence?","options":["will complete","would complete","has completed","would have completed"],"position":13,"type":"multiple_choice","config":{"sat_topic":"Standard English Conventions"},"points":1,"required":true,"group_name":"Form, Structure, and Sense"},{"id":"d9d1e960-f464-4dfc-ae2e-1f918f62566e","test_id":"e4b994df-8f8f-582a-bba2-e53c002d825a","prompt":"The volunteers cleaned the beach, ___ recyclable materials in separate bins. Which choice completes the sentence?","options":["placed","to placing","placing","places"],"position":14,"type":"multiple_choice","config":{"sat_topic":"Standard English Conventions"},"points":1,"required":true,"group_name":"Form, Structure, and Sense"},{"id":"e9fddaa8-45bb-402b-b310-8f259a22e728","test_id":"e4b994df-8f8f-582a-bba2-e53c002d825a","prompt":"The data in the appendix ___ the conclusions of the report. Which choice completes the sentence?","options":["has supported","support","supports","is supporting"],"position":15,"type":"multiple_choice","config":{"sat_topic":"Standard English Conventions"},"points":1,"required":true,"group_name":"Form, Structure, and Sense"},{"id":"cc543d92-5410-441e-9b5a-05c6f292b321","test_id":"e4b994df-8f8f-582a-bba2-e53c002d825a","prompt":"Each of the samples ___ labeled before storage. Which choice completes the sentence?","options":["was","were","have been","are"],"position":16,"type":"multiple_choice","config":{"sat_topic":"Standard English Conventions"},"points":1,"required":true,"group_name":"Form, Structure, and Sense"},{"id":"751caebe-642b-4e42-810a-30cc901803e5","test_id":"e4b994df-8f8f-582a-bba2-e53c002d825a","prompt":"The scientist to ___ the prize was awarded thanked her colleagues. Which choice completes the sentence?","options":["who","whose","which","whom"],"position":17,"type":"multiple_choice","config":{"sat_topic":"Standard English Conventions"},"points":1,"required":true,"group_name":"Form, Structure, and Sense"},{"id":"0fb23c38-bb1f-4720-8924-8dde9a4ebdeb","test_id":"e4b994df-8f8f-582a-bba2-e53c002d825a","prompt":"After adding shaded benches, a park saw more visitors between noon and two. Morning visits remained unchanged.\n\nWhat change did the report directly observe?","options":["An increase in ticket prices.","A decline in overall use.","An increase in midday visits.","A decrease in morning visits."],"position":18,"type":"multiple_choice","config":{"sat_topic":"Information and Ideas"},"points":1,"required":true,"group_name":"Main Ideas and Details"},{"id":"4b5ef1c8-27be-43fa-a1c5-08ca89fe1fec","test_id":"e4b994df-8f8f-582a-bba2-e53c002d825a","prompt":"Two groups read the same article. The group that wrote summaries remembered more details the following week.\n\nWhich conclusion is best supported?","options":["Writing summaries always improves memory.","Writing summaries was associated with better recall.","The groups read different articles.","Both groups forgot the same details."],"position":19,"type":"multiple_choice","config":{"sat_topic":"Information and Ideas"},"points":1,"required":true,"group_name":"Inference