ered evening entry.","Why attendance increased.","Whether attendance changed.","Which day now has free entry."],"position":23,"type":"multiple_choice","config":{"sat_topic":"Information and Ideas"},"points":1,"required":true,"group_name":"Inference"},{"id":"9ae34067-afd1-4b66-ad4c-11ba004f6b05","test_id":"e4b994df-8f8f-582a-bba2-e53c002d825a","prompt":"One explanation for the bird’s decline is that a common insect became harder to find. A second explanation is that suitable nesting sites disappeared.\n\nWhat is the main purpose of the text?","options":["To present two explanations for a decline.","To demonstrate that one explanation is false.","To list the bird’s nesting habits.","To explain how the insect reproduces."],"position":24,"type":"multiple_choice","config":{"sat_topic":"Craft and Structure"},"points":1,"required":true,"group_name":"Text Structure and Purpose"},{"id":"dcb9ff20-0fdb-437d-95cb-f1eaa47f04ce","test_id":"e4b994df-8f8f-582a-bba2-e53c002d825a","prompt":"The new material conducted heat well but cracked after repeated bending. The team recommended it for rigid components.\n\nWhy did the team recommend rigid components?","options":["Rigid components must insulate heat.","The material became more flexible with use.","The team did not test heat conduction.","Repeated bending damaged the material."],"position":25,"type":"multiple_choice","config":{"sat_topic":"Information and Ideas"},"points":1,"required":true,"group_name":"Main Ideas and Details"},{"id":"a244abb8-d165-4b00-b436-d38fffb668a6","test_id":"e4b994df-8f8f-582a-bba2-e53c002d825a","prompt":"Records indicate the building opened in 1890. A photograph dated 1888 shows workers assembling its roof.\n\nWhat does the photograph establish?","options":["Roof construction began after the opening.","The building was demolished in 1888.","Construction was underway before the opening.","The building opened two years earlier than reported."],"position":26,"type":"multiple_choice","config":{"sat_topic":"Information and Ideas"},"points":1,"required":true,"group_name":"Textual Evidence"},{"id":"c329d3ab-e56f-41b1-a033-9eac8907d45a","test_id":"e74e5cb0-f8b8-5c37-bf33-7026c247b906","prompt":"If 3x + 3 = 21, what is x?","options":["6","4","8","10"],"position":0,"type":"multiple_choice","config":{"sat_topic":"Algebra"},"points":1,"required":true,"group_name":"Linear equations"},{"id":"09aae591-5b48-428e-bdec-e9aa68ca4a4d","test_id":"e74e5cb0-f8b8-5c37-bf33-7026c247b906","prompt":"A price of $40 is reduced by 20%. What is the new price in dollars?","options":["30","34","36","32"],"position":1,"type":"multiple_choice","config":{"sat_topic":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis"},"points":1,"required":true,"group_name":"Percentages"},{"id":"3ab04ebd-1861-41d6-a882-aff408a83e74","test_id":"e74e5cb0-f8b8-5c37-bf33-7026c247b906","prompt":"What is the positive solution of x² = 25?","options":[],"position":2,"type":"numeric_answer","config":{"sat_topic":"Advanced Math"},"points":1,"required":true,"group_name":"Quadratic equations"},{"id":"d1fddac4-a31b-4547-a72b-3851348320e0","test_id":"e74e5cb0-f8b8-5c37-bf33-7026c247b906","prompt":"A line passes through (1, 6) and (5, 18). What is its slope?","options":["7","3","1","5"],"position":3,"type":"multiple_choice","config":{"sat_topic":"Algebra"},"points":1,"required":true,"group_name":"Slope"},{"id":"a19b18e5-6f86-4f41-a5b1-8081ea269233","test_id":"e74e5cb0-f8b8-5c37-bf33-7026c247b906","prompt":"A rectangle has width 7 and length 11. What is its area?","options":["77","75","79","81"],"position":4,"type":"multiple_choice","config":{"sat_topic":"Geometry and Trigonometry"},"points":1,"required":true,"group_name":"Area"},{"id":"34f9c731-42b5-48e3-ae8c-8e2bbc5d876e","test_id":"e74e5cb0-f8b8-5c37-bf33-7026c247b906","prompt":"What is the arithmetic mean of 8, 12, 16, and 20?","options":["12","16","18","14"],"position":5,"type":"multiple_choice","config":{"sat_topic":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis"},"points":1,"required":true,"group_name":"M